--- (1) W32 crawl (group QA Smoke Test charter v1.0, orders L254 2026-09-28) ---
W32 = "Provisions on the Administration of Mobile Internet Application Information Services" (Cyberspace Administration of China, promulgated 2022-06-14, effective 2022-08-01, 27 articles, repeals the 2016-06-28 version), official fulltext direct-captured A-grade from cac.gov.cn (2022-06/14/c_1656821626455324.htm; one search hit, one direct get, zero extra negatives). The registry had ZERO prior hits for this regulation, so it is a genuine blank spot rather than a re-crawl.
The finding that changes our own reading: article 2 writes "internet mini-program platform" explicitly into the definition of an APPLICATION DISTRIBUTION service (app stores, quick-app centres, mini-program platforms, browser extension platforms). That puts this company's meta-universe platform on the chapter-3 distribution-platform duty face, while our compliance file so far only modelled the mini-program side as an application PROVIDER. Concretely:
  art.6   provider must real-name-verify registered users (mobile number / ID number / unified social credit code); no real identity -> no service
  art.14  launching a new technology/application/feature with public-opinion or social-mobilisation capacity requires a national-rule security assessment (same direction as W27's 17-article assessment regulation; AIGC features are the obvious instance)
  art.17  distribution platform must file with the provincial CAC within 30 days of going live, with five material groups (operator basics; platform name/domain/access/qualifications/listed categories; licence or filing papers; the art.5 institutional documents; management rules and service agreement)
  art.18  classified management of listed apps, plus filing each app by category
  art.19  composite verification of the listing provider (mobile number + ID number + unified social credit code combined, not a single method) and public display of the provider name and unified social credit code
  art.20  listing and update review must refuse three classes (illegal/undesirable name, icon or blurb; mismatch with the registered real identity; illegal business type); download-count / rating-metric data fabrication and unlawful personal-information collection also bar service; licence and security-assessment status must be verified
  art.21  publish management rules and service agreement; graduated handling (warning / suspension / delisting); keep records and report to the authority
  art.22  conspicuous, convenient complaint-and-report entry with accept/handle/feedback mechanisms
  arts.10/11  security-defect remediation with user notice and authority report; whole-process data-security system and risk monitoring
benchmarks: three-place entry (sec.1 new "platform distribution duty chain" block + sec.3 source row + sec.4 W32 record row; sec.2 gets no new row because the existing 13 rows already carry the criteria face - noted honestly in both the record and the wall). intelligence-wall: W32 dual rows (main + conclusion, R1884 precedent).
consumption: apimarket listing face [arts.19/20: today the only provider identity is a dev_account string handle - no real-name layer, no public-display layer, no three-class review-refusal face = a designable gap that needs no physical item] + launch-ops [art.14 assessment as a launch-gate candidate, art.22 complaint entry] + P-47(3) UGC [art.6 real-name, art.20 unlawful collection] + bootstrap [arts.17/18/21 filing and graduated handling sit in the CEO physical-item domain (registered entity)].
